1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,939
What if your dreams leaked into the morning?

2
00:00:02,979 --> 00:00:05,606
You fall asleep dreaming of a flying whale.

3
00:00:05,646 --> 00:00:07,529
A bubble drifts from your head,

4
00:00:07,569 --> 00:00:09,080
slips through the window,

5
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:10,258
and starts to grow.

6
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:12,615
Morning.

7
00:00:12,655 --> 00:00:15,265
You wake up, and the whale is still there.

8
00:00:15,305 --> 00:00:17,725
It drifts across your bedroom, humming.

9
00:00:17,765 --> 00:00:21,763
Your cat, unimpressed, files this under normal Tuesday activity.

10
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:26,251
In the kitchen, last night's spaghetti dream is raining noodles.

11
00:00:26,291 --> 00:00:28,335
Toast flutters around like birds,

12
00:00:28,375 --> 00:00:31,871
and the fridge keeps humming a lullaby nobody asked for.

13
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:34,987
Outside, everyone's dreams have leaked.

14
00:00:35,027 --> 00:00:37,252
The school bus is a giant banana.

15
00:00:37,292 --> 00:00:39,379
A clock melts over a lamp post,

16
00:00:39,419 --> 00:00:42,674
and a very polite elephant is directing traffic.

17
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:45,492
Then the nightmares start to leak too.

18
00:00:45,532 --> 00:00:48,564
A scribbly monster squeezes out of the neighbor's

19
00:00:48,604 --> 00:00:50,444
dream, towers over the street,

20
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:53,265
and growls, and everyone runs for the bushes.

21
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:55,745
You stand your ground,

22
00:00:55,785 --> 00:00:58,548
take a breath, and offer the monster a hug.

23
00:00:58,588 --> 00:01:00,505
It blinks, shrinks, and purrs.

24
00:01:00,545 --> 00:01:02,135
Nightmares, it turns out,

25
00:01:02,175 --> 00:01:04,678
only stay huge while you run from them.

26
00:01:06,250 --> 00:01:07,607
And here's the twist.

27
00:01:07,647 --> 00:01:09,867
The whale isn't your dream at all.

28
00:01:09,908 --> 00:01:12,195
Gently floating above the rooftops,

29
00:01:12,235 --> 00:01:14,922
it's fast asleep, and in its own enormous

30
00:01:14,962 --> 00:01:16,983
bubble it's dreaming about you.

31
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:20,256
So you climb a ladder of morning light,

32
00:01:20,296 --> 00:01:21,953
hop onto the whale's back,

33
00:01:21,993 --> 00:01:24,369
and sail across the sunrise together.

34
00:01:24,409 --> 00:01:26,131
The dream is leaking, sure.

35
00:01:26,171 --> 00:01:27,502
But so is the wonder.
